       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum for an adult, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision (2,400 mg/day is the more typical ceiling). A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common regimen for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me the clinical reason. I'll add it to the order note."
